## Workflow
- One chat per task. Prefer `claude --worktree <name>` for parallel work.
{%- if enable_superpowers %}
- Brainstorming, planning, TDD, debugging, and code review are handled by the Superpowers plugin's auto-triggered skills (`brainstorming`, `writing-plans`, `subagent-driven-development`, `test-driven-development`, `systematic-debugging`, `superpowers:code-reviewer`). Don't use Claude's native plan mode — Superpowers intercepts it.
- After implementation: `/review-with-superpowers` (delegates to `superpowers:code-reviewer` + the project's `security-auditor`), then `/security-review`, `/commit`, and `/techdebt` at end of session.
{%- else %}
- `/plan` before non-trivial work; skip if you can describe the diff in one sentence.
- Run `/review` before `/commit`. Run `/techdebt` at end of session.
{%- endif %}
- Conventional Commits, one logical change per commit.
